{hi:help geoflow}{...}
{right:{browse "https://github.com/asjadnaqvi/stata-geoflow":geoflow v1.1 (GitHub)}}

{hline}

{title:geoflow}: A Stata module for generating spatial flow arcs.

The package assumes that the users have the following two files:
- {bf:file1}: This file should contain a numeric flow variable defined by {opt from()} and {opt to()} identifiers. The file should already be loaded before using the command.
- {bf:file2}: This file should contain a unique {opt key()} variable, for which coordinates are also defined, and can be merged with {opt from()} and {opt to()} variables.
The node dataset must contain numeric {it:_ID}, {it:_CX}, and {it:_CY} variables. These are generated by default if {opt spshape2dta} is used.

Basic use is as follows:
- use {bf:file1.dta}, clear
- {opt geoflow numvar} using {ul:file2}, {opt from(var)} {opt to(var)} {opt key(var)} {opt save(filename)} {it:[other geoflow options]}

The command will generate a new file that contains the coordinates for the arcs. How these arcs are plotted depends on the user
and it is outside the scope of this command. See GitHub page for examples.



{marker syntax}{title:Syntax}
{p 8 15 2}

{cmd:geoflow} {it:numvar} [{cmd:if} {it:exp}] [{cmd:in} {it:range}] {cmd:using} {it:filename}, {cmd:from}({it:varname}) {cmd:to}({it:varname}) {cmd:key}({it:varname}) {cmd:save}({it:filename}) [{cmd:replace} {cmd:groups}({it:integer}) {cmd:top}({it:integer}) {cmd:points}({it:integer}) {cmd:geoframe} {cmd:radius}({it:real}) {cmd:arrow} {cmd:mark}]

{p 4 4 2}

{synoptset 36 tabbed}{...}
{synopthdr}
{synoptline}

{p2coldent : {opt geoflow numvar} using filename, from(var) to(var) key(var)}The command assumes that the data is already loaded with data containing the
{opt from()} and {opt to()} variables. These variables should contain the identifiers that can be merged with the {it:using} data using the
{opt key()} variable.{p_end}

{pstd}
The variable specified in {opt key()} must exist in the {cmd:using} dataset; it need not exist in the currently loaded flow data.

{p2coldent : {opt points(integer)}}Number of points to generate for each arc. Must be at least 5; default is {opt points(40)}.{p_end}

{p2coldent : {opt save(filename)}}Name of the file that will be saved containing the arc data.{p_end}

{p2coldent : {opt geoframe}}Convert the data to a {stata help geoframe:geoframe}.{p_end}

{p2coldent : {opt replace}}Replace the saved arc dataset if it already exists. With {opt geoframe}, the output frame is always replaced.{p_end}

{p2coldent : {opt groups(integer)}}Number of quantile groups to generate for the {it:numvar} variable. Must be greater than 1.{p_end}

{p2coldent : {opt top(integer)}}Keep the top {opt top()} values from {it:numvar}. Must be greater than 0. This option is recommended if the data contains a very
large number of pairs.{p_end}

{p2coldent : {opt radius(#)}}Shared radius of the arcs, in the same units as the coordinates. If omitted, the radius equals the longest straight-line distance between matched source and destination coordinates after {cmd:if}, {cmd:in}, and {opt top()} selection.
An explicit radius must be positive and at least half that distance (allowing for floating-point tolerance). Smaller radii produce more curved arcs. The radius used is returned in {cmd:r(arcradius)}.
Selected flows with missing coordinates, nonfinite distances, or coincident endpoints must be excluded before generating arcs.{p_end}

{p2coldent : {opt arrow}}Add four arrowhead-coordinate variables ({it:_arrow_y1}, {it:_arrow_x1}, {it:_arrow_y2}, {it:_arrow_x2}) to the saved data. Plot them as a {cmd:pcarrow} layer to show flow direction from {opt from()} to {opt to()}.{p_end}

{pstd}
With {cmd:geoplot}, specify the arrow layer as
{cmd:(pcarrow links, coordinates(_arrow_x1 _arrow_y1 _arrow_x2 _arrow_y2) msize(1.2))}.
The {cmd:coordinates()} option uses X Y order, unlike the positional Y X order of {cmd:twoway pcarrow}.

{pstd}
Control arrowhead size directly with {cmd:msize()} in the {cmd:pcarrow} layer.

{p2coldent : {opt mark}}Generates a variable {it:_mark} in the {opt using} file which equals one for each {opt key()} that
matches with {opt from()} and {opt to()} variables. Other nodes receive missing. This overwrites any existing {it:_mark} and saves the {opt using} file back to disk. Reload existing metadata frames afterward to see the updated marks.{p_end}

{title:Stored results}
{pstd}
{cmd:r(arcradius)} contains the shared radius used to generate the arcs.

{title:Dependencies}
{pstd}
Requires {cmd:arc} from {cmd:graphfunctions}. The optional {cmd:geoframe} integration and map examples additionally require {cmd:geoframe} and {cmd:geoplot}.
{stata ssc install graphfunctions, replace}

{title:Examples}
See {browse "https://github.com/asjadnaqvi/stata-geoflow":GitHub} for examples.

